    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87-a1">

                <pb facs="0168" n="106" xml:id="pg106"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 411.]</seg></opener>
                <head>HARBOR RULES FOR SHANGHAI.</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of changes made by Prince
                        Kung, in his dispatch of January</hi> 31, 1878, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >submitting the rules to the diplomatic body.</hi></p>
                <list>
                    <label>A.</label>
                    <item>—In the last sentence of the covering dispatch, after the words, “and to
                        request that,” the clause, “if they meet your approval,” is inserted.</item>
                    <label>B.</label>
                    <item>—The preamble to the rules was omitted both from the original and the
                        amended dispatches.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed>CHESTER HOLCOMBE.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-02-23"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 23,
                        1878</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
